      "writtenOn": "2022-08-01T21:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Simply comparing against user-entered strings makes it easy for typos to creep in.  For example, if someone put in `fuzzing_frameworks: [\"afl++\"],` there would be no error, but their fuzzer would never be enabled.  Its often more user-friendly to use individual properties, for example something like:\n```\nfuzzing_frameowrks: {\n    afl: false,\n}\n```\n\nThat would also let you default all of the frameworks to true, and then disable the ones you don\u0027t want.  That will help later if you add a third framework, with your list of strings you would have to add the new framework to every module that set the `fuzzing_frameworks` property.",
      "revId": "7315a5137de1b0bd30c361cf4da9740ee7513b86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
